  "notes": "Governmental funds are cash basis (Exhibits C-E, Total Governmental Funds 2025 column on p6); beginning cash 193,387 and ending cash 166,383 are the total fund balances (all cash). Business-type funds are accrual basis (Exhibits G-H, Totals 2025 column); measure is net position; proprietary cash-flow field left null because basis is cash (accrual SCF is on p9). Taxes 92,747 split using Statement of Activities general revenues (p2): property tax 51,912, motor vehicle tax 7,313, sales tax 33,522; items add to the line. Debt service 20,349 split into principal 15,000, interest 5,260 and operating expenditures 89 per Schedule 4 (p14); the 89 is placed with debt service interest (review). The Fire fund's payment of long-term debt principal 1,357 and interest 1,585, printed under Other financing sources (uses) below total expenditures, are recorded as debt service disbursements with outside_printed_total (other_financing null). Business-type receipts = total operating revenue 331,517 + interest income 2,688; disbursements = total operating expenses 323,151 (incl. depreciation 76,267) + interest paid on long term debt 5,772; transfer to other funds (16,400) is transfers_net. Exhibit B (p2) heading says year ended September 30, 2024 but figures are 2025 and agree with the exhibits. Balance sheet is Exhibit A Totals 2025 (governmental modified cash plus business-type accrual). Detail: Schedules 1-4 (p10-14); Schedule 5 (p15, combined budget summary by fund type): only its Proprietary receipts and disbursements lines are recorded in detail (no other schedule covers the utility funds; budgetary cash basis), with no detail_totals entry since its totals mix fund types; its General and Special Revenue lines are not recorded to avoid double counting with Schedules 1-4; no budget columns on schedules 1-4 so budget_final null; zero-valued lines other than General Fund capital outlay were skipped. Read pages 1-15 of 15",
  "report_discrepancies": [
